// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`LaneBlueprintView > matches the Receive Shipment blueprint snapshot 1`] = `
<div>
  <div
    style="display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: baseline; flex-wrap: wrap;"
  >
    <h2
      style="margin: 0px;"
    >
      Receive Shipment
    </h2>
    <span
      class="badge"
    >
      v
      1
       · 
      draft
    </span>
    <span
      style="color: var(--text-muted);"
    >
      Runs on 
      purchase_order
    </span>
  </div>
  <p>
    Receive a shipment for one purchase order: verify the delivery, record what arrived, stage and put away the stock, and close the order. One run per purchase order. The discrepancy branch sends a short or damaged receipt to the Warehouse Manager for review. This is the Receive Shipment lane from Part B of the Process Lane spec, with the ADR-0023 changes applied: entered values are stored in run data (steps 1.1 and 1.2), record steps call governed Action Types, the hold branch has a declared exit (record the hold, end with outcome held), the workflow actions it replaces are declared (wf-wh-01 on step 4.2, wf-wh-07 on step 2B.1), and the per-line steps repeat over the order lines. The spec's hybrid 'form + record' steps are split (ADR-0024 section 3): 3.1 assigns the staging bin and 3.2 posts the receipt moves; 3.3 confirms the put-away bins and 3.4 posts the put-away moves. Action Type ids are provisional until WP-0705 adopts them (ADR-0024 section 14).
  </p>
  <p
    style="color: var(--text-muted);"
  >
    Starts when 
    $record.status equals "OPEN"
    .
  </p>
  <h3>
    Stages
  </h3>
  <div
    aria-label="Stage order"
    style="display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 16px;"
  >
