      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section
    style="margin-bottom: 20px;"
  >
    <h3>
      Run data
    </h3>
    <p
      style="color: var(--text-muted);"
    >
      Values the lane collects as it runs, declared up front - every entered value lands here or on the record, never nowhere.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>
            Field
          </th>
          <th>
            Type
          </th>
          <th>
            Required
          </th>
          <th>
            Per line
          </th>
          <th>
            What it holds
          </th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>
              carrier
            </code>
          </td>
          <td>
            string
          </td>
          <td>
            Yes
          </td>
          <td>
            No
          </td>
          <td>
            Carrier who delivered the shipment, entered at step 1.1.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>
              delivery_note_number
            </code>
          </td>
          <td>
            string
          </td>
          <td>
            Yes
          </td>
          <td>
            No
          </td>
          <td>
            Delivery-note number from the carrier's paperwork, entered at step 1.1.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>
              received_date
            </code>
          </td>
          <td>
            date
          </td>
          <td>
            Yes
          </td>
          <td>
            No
          </td>
          <td>
            Date the shipment arrived, entered at step 1.1. Must match the PO's expected date.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>
              delivery_note_qty
            </code>
          </td>
          <td>
            integer
          </td>
          <td>
            Yes
          </td>
          <td>
            Yes
          </td>
          <td>
            Quantity on the delivery note, per order line, entered at step 1.2. Keyed by line id.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>
              rejection_reason
            </code>
          </td>
          <td>
            string
          </td>
          <td>
            No
          </td>
          <td>
            Yes
          </td>
          <td>
            Rejection reason, per order line, entered at step 2.1 when units are rejected. Keyed by line id.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>
              staging_bin
            </code>
          </td>
          <td>
            string
          </td>
          <td>
            Yes
          </td>
          <td>
            No
          </td>
          <td>
            Receiving bin the goods are staged in (RCV-01 or RCV-02), entered at step 3.1.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>
              putaway_bin
            </code>
          </td>
          <td>
            string
          </td>
          <td>
            Yes
          </td>
          <td>
            Yes
          </td>
          <td>
            Put-away bin, per order line, confirmed at step 3.3. Suggested by the Receiving Agent from the product's preferred bin. Keyed by line id.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>
              hold_reason
            </code>
          </td>
          <td>
            string
          </td>
          <td>
            No
          </td>
          <td>
            No
          </td>
          <td>
            Why the receipt is held, entered at step 2B.2 when the manager rejects the discrepancy.
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
  <section
    style="margin-bottom: 20px;"
  >
    <h3>
      Mapped record fields
    </h3>
    <p
      style="color: var(--text-muted);"
    >
      Fields a step writes straight onto the anchor record. The blueprint names the mapping, never a record's values.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>
            Field
          </th>
          <th>
            Step
          </th>
          <th>
            Maps to
          </th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>
            Quantity received
          </td>
          <td>
            Enter received quantities
          </td>
          <td>
            <code>
              record.lines[].qty_received
            </code>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            Quantity rejected
          </td>
          <td>
            Enter received quantities
          </td>
          <td>
            <code>
              record.lines[].qty_rejected
            </code>
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
  <p
    style="color: var(--text-muted);"
  >
    This blueprint shows the lane definition only - no run, no record data.
  </p>
</div>
